  "description": "CAQVUP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H61 Eu1 N4 O33 Si8 Tb3 1-,4(C2 H6 O1),C8 H20 N1 1+. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors; Eu2? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.509-4.980 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.98-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [NEt4][(Ph4Si4O8)2(Tb3Eu)(NO3)4(OH)(EtOH)3(H2O)]·4(EtOH). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II), I(II).",
